SECTION (d): liveness through chains
========================================================================

--- dead-through-two-call-levels
  F(A) = G(A, H(F(['a'/'ba'][''/'aa'][''/'aab'][''/'aaba']('aa' ['ba'/'a']A)), A))
  G(A, B) = A
  H(A, B) = A
  main = F(X)
  S* = [('F', 0), ('G', 0), ('H', 0)]
  (note: (H,1) and (H,2) are live *in H*, but the only call to H
   sits in G's dead argument 2, so neither is ever forced)
  live unfolding E' = X
  lazy == E' on all inputs, eager diverges: OK

--- fixpoint deadness through two definitions
  P(A) = Q(M(A))
  Q(A) = A
  M(A) = K(A)
  K(A) = 'a'
  main = P(X)
  S* = [('Q', 0)]  (expect exactly {(Q,0)}; (P,0),(M,0),(K,0) dead)
  live unfolding E' = 'a'
  lazy == E' == eager == 'a' on all inputs (P,Q,M,K all agree; only the deadness chain matters here): OK

